[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ServiceResource" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Economy/ServiceResource.cs" id="1_service"]

; Bryn's order bench (Phase 38Q) — the master's commission counter. He makes anything the player
; already knows how to make at a forge, and SUPPLIES WHATEVER THEY DID NOT BRING at his own counter
; price, on top of this fee for his hands.
;
; ⚠️ THE MATERIALS ARE THE WHOLE FEATURE, AND WITHOUT THEM THIS FILE SHOULD NOT EXIST. StationForge
; stands eight metres from this bench and is FREE. A master who charged for labour on a recipe the
; player can already supply would be strictly worse than walking over to it — correct, validated,
; saved and completely imperceptible, which is the failure that got 38G parked. What is being sold
; here is not having to go and dig up three iron ingots.
;
; ⚠️ PRICED, AND --validate ENFORCES THAT IT IS PRICED — the opposite of the last three services to
; ship. 38O's search, 38P's collect counter and 38P2's appraisal are all forced FREE because
; ServiceRules refuses an unaffordable service before the verb runs, so a fee fails closed on exactly
; the player who needs the counter. A commission hands over GOODS, so the same reasoning inverts: a
; free master is the realm's materials shop with the spread deleted. Do not "correct" this to 0.
;
; PriceGold 60 — the labour, and it is the only thing standing between the game and an unbounded gold
; loop. Buy the materials from Bryn, have him make the piece, sell the piece: unlike every earlier
; price in the economy the ShopPricing clamps CANNOT close that, because a commission spans two
; different items and crafting is meant to add value. Only one recipe in the realm is anywhere near
; it, and these numbers are --validate's own rather than reasoned out: dropped to a fee of 1, the
; single failure printed is
;
;   recipe.kit.alchemy  materials 69 at Allied standing, and the smith pays 81 for the kit
;
; so the floor is a fee above 12. Every other forge recipe stayed silent even at a fee of 1: the
; gear ones cost far more in materials than the piece fetches, which is crafting working as intended.
;
; 60 is chosen well clear of that floor rather than on it, because the margin an author leaves is the
; margin a later recipe, a keener buyer or a new specialty removes — and --validate checks it in both
; directions every boot, at Allied standing, which is the cheapest corner the loop could open at.
; 60 is also roughly two thirds of a steel sword's shelf price, which is the feel wanted:
; commissioning undercuts buying the finished piece off his shelf in exact proportion to what the
; player already carries, and never by enough to be worth doing for its own sake.
;
; MaterialsShopId is his own shop rather than a second markup field, so his standing discount and his
; metal specialty reach a commission exactly as they reach his shelf — one ramp, not two. ⚠️ He is
; NOT required to stock what he supplies: commission materials come out of the back, and requiring
; stock would mean the day he sold out he also stopped being able to make anything.
;
; CommissionStation Forge (1). What he will make is what the player knows at a forge — no second list
; is authored, because CraftingPanel and CraftingComponent.Knows already answer that question and a
; second answer is a second thing to keep in step.
;
; ⚠️ A SEPARATE INTERACTABLE FROM BRYN HIMSELF, AND IT HAS TO BE. An entity gets one interactable
; (ServiceComponent's own warning) and he carries a DialogueComponent — his conversation holds a quest
; and his shop. So the order bench stands on its own beside him, which is 38P2's appraiser shape and
; 38P's broker-and-clerk split for the same reason: you talk to the man and you leave an order at the
; bench.
;
; No flag of any kind. Commissioning is repeatable by nature and answers "nothing to do" from what the
; player knows, exactly as the warden's search answers it from the pack.

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_service")
Id = "service.ember_crown.commission"
NameKey = "service.ember_crown.commission.name"
Kind = 9
PriceGold = 60
FactionId = "faction.villagers"
UnlockFlagId = ""
RestHour = 8
XpReward = 0
GrantedFlagId = ""
ReputationDelta = 0
CommissionStation = 1
MaterialsShopId = "shop.ember_crown.smith"
